SUMMARY:Flat Laurel Creek Rock Scramble
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis is one of the most popular cr
 eek scrambles near Asheville. Note this is not the Flat Laurel Creek Trail
 \, it is a creek hike. It begins at NC Hwy. 215 near the confluence of Fla
 t Laurel Creek and the West Fork of the Pigeon River (35.3285\, -82.9096)\
 , approximately\, at about 9:30. We will ascend past numerous rapids and i
 mpressive waterfalls. We will be in the creek or rock hopping most of the 
 day. The requirements are a good sense of balance\, comfortable shoes with
  good traction\, and ability or interest to scramble up rocks in a creek. 
 We'll also climb a steep trace trail *around* the highest waterfall. Good 
 swimming holes abound. The pace will be moderate\, with time for pictures\
 , and we will take a short break at one of the many scenic spots for lunch
 . After finishing the ascent we will trail hike up to the Black Balsam/Big
  Sam parking lot\, where cars will be left for this shuttle. You will have
  the option to hike up Big Sam Mountain (over 6K) for the view. However\, 
 the group will proceed directly to the parking lot for Big Sam.\nWe will c
 limb 950 feet and hike approx. 3.5 miles.\nWe will be meeting at the end o
 f Black Balsam Knob Road (FS 816) at the parking lot for the Big Sam trail
 head at 9:05 am. The coordinates are 35.325586\, -82.881986.\nAny question
 s I can be reached or text at 828 231-3581.\n\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Ashevill
 e Hiking Group (AHG) event involves serious risks\, including but not limi
 ted to: slipping or falling on wet rocks\; sprains\, fractures\, and other
  injuries from falls\; water-related injury\; exposure to weather\, cold\,
  or heat\; wildlife encounters\; remote locations with limited or delayed 
 access to emergency medical care\; and risks arising from my own or other 
 participants' actions. These risks cannot be eliminated regardless of care
  taken. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that 
 they have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and
  supplies. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assu
 re your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full responsib
 ility for any damages\, losses\, or injuries.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316362291
 /
