SUMMARY:Scenic AVL Wildcard - Asheville Camino
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Overview:** This hike is offered
  as a monthly training hike with the WNC Asheville Chapter of the associat
 ion of American Pilgrims on the Camino. The route has been announced on th
 e WNC Camino Group [Facebook Group Page](https://www.facebook.com/groups/A
 VLCamino/announcements).\n\nSee details here: [https://www.facebook.com/sh
 are/p/1DSW8LYBvx/](https://www.facebook.com/share/p/1DSW8LYBvx/)\n\n**12 M
 ile Route**\nIsaiah will be leading the full 12 mile route around west Ash
 eville through Malvern Hills and back along Haywood. Isaiah and his wife c
 reated the route many years ago when they were training for their first Ca
 mino. It's amazing to see how the tradition of urban hiking has grown in A
 sheville as a result of their original training hikes. Here is the route t
 hat Isaiah will lead: [https://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/avl
 -camino-frances-west-loop-7bb5b06?u=i&sh=ifwm3x](https://www.alltrails.com
 /explore/custom-routes/avl-camino-frances-west-loop-7bb5b06?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)
 \n\n**7 Mile Route**\nI will be leading the shorter option of 6.75 miles\,
  which will start with the full group\, and then turn up the road that ove
 rlooks the French Broad River. We will stop for coffee at Wrong Way Campgr
 ound at the 3.4 mile mark.\nAll Trails Route for SHORTER option: [https://
 www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/copy-avl-camino-frances-west-loop-
 3645ccb?u=i&sh=ifwm3x ](https://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/co
 py-avl-camino-frances-west-loop-3645ccb?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\n**Elevation Gain
 : 600 ft**\nBoth routes have about the same elevation gain (down to the ri
 ver and back).\n\n**What to bring:**\nPayment method for coffee or snacks.
  For the longer hike\, there will be a brief lunch stop near a market wher
 e you can buy a sandwich or eat a sandwich you bring with you. Carry adequ
 ate water.\n\n**There are NO BATHROOMS at the start\, so plan accordingly.
 **\n\nThis hike will count as a weekend wildcard on my Scenic Asheville se
 ries. There are 9 hikes in the series\; hike them all and receive an attra
 ctive badge for your backpack.\n\nGuests: This is a good hike to bring a g
 uest\, because it's not as hard as some others. If you bring a guest\, rem
 ind me of their name at the end so that they will get credit for the hike.
 \n\n**Camino FAQ**\nThe Camino de Santiago is an Unesco world heritage rou
 te followed by pilgrims for centuries. If you are unfamiliar with the Cami
 no\, here are a few links to learn more:\n\\*[American Pilgrims on the Cam
 ino](https://americanpilgrims.org/iwpmap_directory/western-north-carolina/
 )\n\n* [Stingy Nomads Camino](https://stingynomads.com/camino-de-santiago-
 walking-guide/)\n\\*[Gronze Camino Planner](https://www.gronze.com/)\n\nWh
 en we stop for coffee\, you can ask all the questions you want.\n\nDisclai
 mer and Release of Liability:\nThis activity involves hiking on city stree
 ts that may have traffic. Participants are responsible for their safety on
  streets and trails. The organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a p
 rofessional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this 
 trip. If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you
  freely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\
 , and damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this eve
 nt. In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: [htt
 ps://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316363699
 /
