SUMMARY:Sleepy Gap--Lake Powhatan  8 miles\, 1300'
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nDescription: Hike from the Blue Ri
 dge Parkway\, along the Mountain-to-Sea trail\, through Bent Creek and aro
 und Lake Powhatan\, then back to the BRP. Good footing\; mostly wide trail
 s\; some nearby creeks\; nice view from Sleepy Gap. From Sleepy Gap south 
 on the MST via Chestnut Cove to Explorer and Pine Tree loops. Then circle 
 the Lake and have a snack at the picnic tables. Ascend via Small Creek and
  Deerfield Connector to the unmarked Stambaugh trail and the MST back to S
 leepy Gap. Type: Loop. Max elev: 3200’. Avg moving pace: 2.4 mph. Diffic
 ulty (1=effortless\, 10=hard): 6. Well behaved dogs on a leash are OK\n**(
 Possibility of lunch following the hike at the Stone Ridge Tavern)**\n\\*\
 \***Courtesy** (Please read carefully!)\\*\\* Only sign up if you \\\\\\*t
 ruly\\\\\\* plan to come. If you must cancel\, please change your status t
 o "Not Going" as soon as possible. Avoid dropping out within 24 hours of t
 he hike so that wait-listers can have sufficient notice. And please please
  PLEASE don't be a no-show\n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group even
 t involves hiking and\, possibly\, transportation to and from the meetup s
 ite. Participants are responsible for their own safety and affirm that the
 y have the appropriate skills\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and su
 pplies. Hiking may involve risks to oneself and property. Neither your hik
 e organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group can assure your safety nor eliminat
 e all risks. Participants assume full responsibility for any injuries\, da
 mages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/316400633
 /
